<service>
  <!--
    MSCMS v14 — WinSW v3 service definition for the WATCHDOG (service orchestrator).
    ============================================================
    This is the PRIMARY carrier. The watchdog process owns and health-checks
    every sub-service below (it spawns them detached, probes TCP + HTTP, and
    auto-restarts any that die). Wrapping the watchdog in WinSW gives the WHOLE
    tree process-level auto-recovery (Restart on failure), with NO risk of
    double-launching a service (which would otherwise fight the watchdog's
    single-instance lock on :3011 or the per-port LISTENING ownership).

    Install (see README.md):
      1. Rename the WinSW binary to mscms-watchdog.exe and drop it next to this file.
      2. mscms-watchdog.exe install
      3. Open services.msc -> set "Log On" to your interactive account (.\AS) so the
         service inherits the same environment as your session (localhost proxy :10808,
         D:\ paths, C:\Users\AS\...). Do NOT put the  in this XML.
      4. mscms-watchdog.exe start
  -->
  <id>mscms-watchdog</id>
  <name>MSCMS v14 Watchdog (Service Orchestrator)</name>
  <description>
    WinSW carrier for the MSCMS v14 watchdog. The watchdog owns and health-checks all
    sub-services: 3002 main (server.js @ D:\MSCMS-Desktop\resources), 3005 nurture
    (tumblr-nurture-server.js), 3010 content-gen (content-gen/service.js), 8001 kkmatch
    (D:\kk-match-backend\.venv\Scripts\pythonw.exe _run.py), 3307 MySQL (tcpOnly),
    8080 MPT (uvicorn @ D:\MoneyPrinterTurbo), 20779 exit-guard, 3012 visitor-profile,
    3013 desktop-sync. WinSW gives the watchdog itself Restart-on-failure recovery.
  </description>

  <!-- Node interpreter. The watchdog re-resolves the newest node for its children;
       this path only needs to be *a* working node. Update if node is upgraded. -->
  <executable>C:\Users\AS\\binaries\node\versions\22.22.2-6\node.exe</executable>
  <arguments>tools\mscms-watchdog.js</arguments>
  <workingdirectory>C:\Users\AS\WorkBuddy\2026-06-13-19-42-19</workingdirectory>

  <priority>Normal</priority>
  <startmode>Automatic</startmode>
  <stoptimeout>30 sec</stoptimeout>

  <logpath>D:\mscms-ws\logs\winsw</logpath>
  <log mode="roll-by-size">
    <sizeThreshold>10240</sizeThreshold>
    <keepFiles>8</keepFiles>
  </log>

  <!-- Recovery: restart on first/second/third failure, then keep retrying. -->
  <onfailure action="restart" delay="10 sec"/>
  <onfailure action="restart" delay="30 sec"/>
  <onfailure action="restart" delay="60 sec"/>
  <resetfailure>3600 sec</resetfailure>

  <!--
    SECURITY: intentionally NO <serviceaccount> with a .
    After `install`, set the Log On account to .\AS in services.msc (or via
    `sc config mscms-watchdog obj= ".\AS" = "***"`). LocalSystem also
    works for D: + localhost but may lack ACLs to user-scoped resources.
  -->
</service>
